Denmark registry-first diagnostic corpus

Danmarks Adresseregister (DAR), Klimadatastyrelsen, with addresses and road names
maintained by the Danish municipalities; distributed through Datafordeleren.
https://datafordeler.dk/dataoversigt/danmarks-adresseregister-dar/dar-fildownload

© Klimadatastyrelsen. Licensed under CC BY 4.0:
https://datafordeler.dk/vejledning/brugervilkaar/danmarks-adresseregister-dar/
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This corpus is a sampled, joined, projected and reformatted adaptation. The
municipalities and Klimadatastyrelsen have not endorsed it. Data is supplied
without warranties under the source license. The source-code license does not
replace the data terms.

The pinned source is DAR v4 Current JSON, generation 787. Expectations use the
house number's linked access point, not a road point or a unit's door point.
Published floor/door variants check building recovery, not apartment identity.
Points have distinct technical/accuracy classes; no surveyed entrance accuracy
or nationwide success rate is claimed. Shared DAR ancestry with index inputs
limits independence. See docs/evaluation/registry/dk.md for preparation,
selection, provenance and limitations.
